{"posts":[{"id":"aboutcompression_p31_751","t":"Hi Paul,\n\nSorry if my bad English had confused you.\n\nAs far as I understand, CP means and bullish or bearish that taken balance order. Meaning all order had been consumed and when price back to CP zone, the price will up/down all the way.\n\nHope I can explain well in below pic.","a":"boy2boy","d":"","n":"#751","p":31,"im":["fbc91c63a71e44888edfdb4024ec3a7441ad00dc"],"m":751},{"id":"aboutcompression_p31_752","t":"boy2boy wrote: Hi Paul,\n\nSorry if my bad English had confused you.\n\nAs far as I understand, CP means and bullish or bearish that taken balance order. Meaning all order had been consumed and when price back to CP zone, the price will up/down all the way.\n\nHope I can explain well in below pic.\n\nThat's correct, so why did you mark as CP areas that were NOT CP? Like in this chart of yours:","a":"Les_Paul","d":"","n":"#752","p":31,"im":["f00a89fb49daf2ca50faa36055d7fc7958cae56f"],"m":752},{"id":"aboutcompression_p31_753","t":"Hi,\n\nActually, it is quite confuse for me when finding on that chart.\n\nSome I'd identified the pull back / balance consumed.\n\nDuring the bullish, some as you drew on it, were not being test, fresh zone.\n\nSo, for this long bullish, I do not know if it is a CP... or only partly CP.","a":"boy2boy","d":"","n":"#753","p":31,"im":[],"m":753},{"id":"aboutcompression_p31_754","t":"Les_Paul wrote:\n\nboy2boy wrote: Hi Paul,\n\nSorry if my bad English had confused you.\n\nAs far as I understand, CP means and bullish or bearish that taken balance order. Meaning all order had been consumed and when price back to CP zone, the price will up/down all the way.\n\nHope I can explain well in below pic.\n\nlovely example LP if you mark your bases like LP, then you can see when price came back to take the orders there before advancing, hence your CP much easier that way when you start. later you wont have to do that, but for now it can be good \"training wheels\"","a":"Harry","d":"","n":"#754","p":31,"im":["f00a89fb49daf2ca50faa36055d7fc7958cae56f"],"m":754},{"id":"aboutcompression_p31_755","t":"Hi Harry / Paul,\n\nPriced dropped when hit Supply Zone.\n\nCan I assume the price will touch the fresh demand if it would like to continue bullish?\n\nOr it need to touch another supply on top of current before it drop.","a":"boy2boy","d":"","n":"#755","p":31,"im":[],"m":755},{"id":"aboutcompression_p31_756","t":"Hi,\n\nPrice dropped nicely from supply. I'm trying to get the feeling from live/current price action.","a":"boy2boy","d":"","n":"#756","p":31,"im":["4f6816e1e514f5513e2cadc8c5eaa82bba889429"],"m":756},{"id":"aboutcompression_p31_757","t":"boy2boy wrote: Hi,\n\nPrice dropped nicely from supply. I'm trying to get the feeling from live/current price action.\n\nYes, it dropped because the price was COMPRESSED... did you notice?\n\nwhy don't you take a few charts and mark correct compression zones?\n\nLP","a":"Les_Paul","d":"","n":"#757","p":31,"im":["4f6816e1e514f5513e2cadc8c5eaa82bba889429"],"m":757},{"id":"aboutcompression_p31_758","t":"Hi,","a":"boy2boy","d":"","n":"#758","p":31,"im":["34c4a313af2f2f35e39d68383f6920780bcb9b4d"],"m":758},{"id":"aboutcompression_p31_759","t":"boy2boy wrote: Hi,\n\nOk, that's COMPRESSION, well done","a":"Les_Paul","d":"","n":"#759","p":31,"im":["34c4a313af2f2f35e39d68383f6920780bcb9b4d"],"m":759},{"id":"aboutcompression_p31_760","t":"Hi,\n\nIt looks like more easy to identify CP in lower TF...","a":"boy2boy","d":"","n":"#760","p":31,"im":["211e3457c032b04bb00f7bcbe655f25bd77b32ad"],"m":760},{"id":"aboutcompression_p31_761","t":"Hi,","a":"boy2boy","d":"","n":"#761","p":31,"im":["0d2703c46bb9e2fb93419715525f54877ab0ad19"],"m":761},{"id":"aboutcompression_p31_762","t":"boy2boy wrote: Hi,\n\nHi, I cannot see any marked CP in your last chart...","a":"Les_Paul","d":"","n":"#762","p":31,"im":["0d2703c46bb9e2fb93419715525f54877ab0ad19"],"m":762},{"id":"aboutcompression_p31_763","t":"Hi,","a":"boy2boy","d":"","n":"#763","p":31,"im":["06a6833b2f36498c63a54de12000c8b1a4bfeeb6"],"m":763},{"id":"aboutcompression_p31_764","t":"You got me!!! My bad on that...","a":"boy2boy","d":"","n":"#764","p":31,"im":[],"m":764},{"id":"aboutcompression_p31_765","t":"Hi,","a":"boy2boy","d":"","n":"#765","p":31,"im":["4c9aa7fc3d173bea4f183c7b2a5183159b9dae69"],"m":765},{"id":"aboutcompression_p31_766","t":"Hi,","a":"boy2boy","d":"","n":"#766","p":31,"im":["18c3dc7396860064df40b9fd3e58f11882cdd17f"],"m":766},{"id":"aboutcompression_p31_767","t":"Hi,","a":"boy2boy","d":"","n":"#767","p":31,"im":["7bab84256ca917f4589ab9103cd627fd54d247ef"],"m":767},{"id":"aboutcompression_p31_768","t":"Hi,","a":"boy2boy","d":"","n":"#768","p":31,"im":["3e4dba3dc12cb155e1f582369a6bcb69458473da"],"m":768},{"id":"aboutcompression_p31_769","t":"boy2boy wrote: Hi,\n\nThank you B2B!\n\nNow that you are perfectly able to identify consumed zones, it is time to proceed to the next step:\n\nAre you aware of the standard marking of Compressed Zones? Pls start using it. You will see that the charts will start to be much better-arranged.\n\nSomething like this:\n\nShow a couple of charts and then we can go on to the next step\n\nLes_Paul","a":"Les_Paul","d":"","n":"#769","p":31,"im":["3e4dba3dc12cb155e1f582369a6bcb69458473da","fdecf8ceb24de74ebc1dba1fba7e2ae9c8c1d2d9"],"m":769},{"id":"aboutcompression_p31_770","t":"boy2boy wrote: Hi,\n\nHi, CP marked by green arrows, the arrow is to help show in which direction we want price to travel along through the marked CP (+ my screengrab software doesnt have lines without arrow )\n\ni think using your boxes to mark bases and see if they have been visited does help you see the CP, very soon you wont need them","a":"Harry","d":"","n":"#770","p":31,"im":["2460742940295e8a612373db87e1e3144037c48e","ce604049ad9a7f7aa7b3ad108b34ed7772023ce3"],"m":770},{"id":"aboutcompression_p31_771","t":"Hi,\n\nAre you aware of the standard marking of Compressed Zones? Pls start using it.\n\nHope I'm doing it correctly.","a":"boy2boy","d":"","n":"#771","p":31,"im":["523c65b7c34855fe1f0959f5e396b9b6ca3cf43c"],"m":771},{"id":"aboutcompression_p31_772","t":"Hi,","a":"boy2boy","d":"","n":"#772","p":31,"im":["c0e0b3ca665eb7b31c4c0e684d6961dbff44518f"],"m":772},{"id":"aboutcompression_p31_773","t":"Hi,","a":"boy2boy","d":"","n":"#773","p":31,"im":["9b7e5a688ce7ad5db634457cf442d0f75e3a4ab9"],"m":773},{"id":"aboutcompression_p31_774","t":"Hi,","a":"boy2boy","d":"","n":"#774","p":31,"im":["67dd60c98c65d4719a3f85fb18249b5862ef1214"],"m":774},{"id":"aboutcompression_p31_775","t":"boy2boy wrote: Hi,\n\nAre you aware of the standard marking of Compressed Zones? Pls start using it.\n\nHope I'm doing it correctly.\n\nit was only for demonstration purposes, i wont do it again, i promise","a":"Harry","d":"","n":"#775","p":31,"im":[],"m":775}],"images":[{"k":"fbc91c63a71e44888edfdb4024ec3a7441ad00dc","t":"assets/thumbs/fbc91c63a71e44888edfdb4024ec3a7441ad00dc.webp","f":"assets/images/fbc91c63a71e44888edfdb4024ec3a7441ad00dc.png","w":1263,"h":629,"b":18950,"o":"fbc91c63a71e44888edfdb4024ec3a7441ad00dc.png","p":31,"pid":"aboutcompression_p31_751"},{"k":"f00a89fb49daf2ca50faa36055d7fc7958cae56f","t":"assets/thumbs/f00a89fb49daf2ca50faa36055d7fc7958cae56f.webp","f":"assets/images/f00a89fb49daf2ca50faa36055d7fc7958cae56f.png","w":1263,"h":629,"b":19286,"o":"f00a89fb49daf2ca50faa36055d7fc7958cae56f.png","p":31,"pid":"aboutcompression_p31_754"},{"k":"4f6816e1e514f5513e2cadc8c5eaa82bba889429","t":"assets/thumbs/4f6816e1e514f5513e2cadc8c5eaa82bba889429.webp","f":"assets/images/4f6816e1e514f5513e2cadc8c5eaa82bba889429.png","w":1263,"h":629,"b":15434,"o":"4f6816e1e514f5513e2cadc8c5eaa82bba889429.png","p":31,"pid":"aboutcompression_p31_757"},{"k":"34c4a313af2f2f35e39d68383f6920780bcb9b4d","t":"assets/thumbs/34c4a313af2f2f35e39d68383f6920780bcb9b4d.webp","f":"assets/images/34c4a313af2f2f35e39d68383f6920780bcb9b4d.png","w":1263,"h":629,"b":16870,"o":"34c4a313af2f2f35e39d68383f6920780bcb9b4d.png","p":31,"pid":"aboutcomp